1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:10,223
Supabase is the primary image store. R2 holds a mirrored copy with the
same object key.

2
00:00:10,223 --> 00:00:21,175
The real API supplies a Supabase URL. The browser loads the primary
image successfully.

3
00:00:21,175 --> 00:00:34,336
Only this browser blocks Supabase image requests. The application
automatically retries the same object in R2.

4
00:00:34,336 --> 00:00:53,504
No immediate error: the 10-second image deadline triggers the same R2
fallback automatically.

5
00:00:53,504 --> 00:01:04,486
Remove the browser block and reload. A fresh image load uses Supabase
again.

6
00:01:04,486 --> 00:01:15,560
Automatic image-read fallback works. The database and API remain online
throughout this simulation.
